<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elbasan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Scampa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elbasan is a city in central Albania on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkumbin">Shkumbin</a> river. As Roman Scampa it was a station on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-egnatia">Via Egnatia</a>, the road across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> from the Adriatic to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. In 1466 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> built a fortress there during his campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, and the town grew into an Ottoman trading and craft centre. It remains one of the largest cities of Albania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elbasan.jpg" alt="Elbasan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pasztilla aka Attila Terbócs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elbasan,_Albania,_St_Mary%27s_Church_2018_07.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
